Z||000000||dodger||06-21-2000||12:30 AM||||So what can be causing high idle!?<BR>Codes 24 & 35 are showing.That's idle air(?) control, and speed sensor. It idles at 1800 when driving normaly...and settles down to 1100 if stopped for a few minutes. Idiot light comes on a few times a day. <BR>Here's some history: <BR>last week, before this started, it was failing to start at random times...then the ignition module was changed...it ran smoother and seemed to fix the problem...but on the way home the idle suddenly went to 2000 and the light came on. Brought it back the next time and it showed the above codes. The Idle air control was changed and the idle was perfect...almost rock solid at 1100 where I wanted it...then halfway home it did it again...!!!<BR>Any ideas?   Is it possibly related to the ignition module problem, or coincidence it started when the module was changed?  (it could still randomly fail to start as before, it's been less than a week).<BR>Thanks for any thoughts... and thanks for reading this far... <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ROB MAC||06-21-2000||01:21 AM||||Mine did that and then mysteriously stopped doing it. I know my TPS was giving some slightly abnormal voltages so I suspect the answer might be there. Please post the solution to yours if you find it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||06-21-2000||01:48 AM||||This may be a silly response, but have you checked the simple things first...like the EGR and EGR tube? Also, dirty a dirty throttle body has been known to cause idle problems. Thats the only things I can think of right off the top of my head. May sound over simplified, but worth a check!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mattsfiero||06-21-2000||01:59 AM||||Well dodger I have recently got my Idle down and yes code 35 is the IAC valve....all I had to do is clean it out and the Idle droppe down to about 900-950...try this first and let me know how you made out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||2
